WEBVTT

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:06.920
What's wrong?

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.080
My mom put green peppers in my lunch again.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.960
I'll get in trouble if I don't eat them.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.540
Ugh.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.000
Show some appreciation.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:27.790
HUH?!

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.540
Appreciation for you suddenly eating my lunch?

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.170
But you hate green peppers, right?

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.630
Well, yeah...

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.170
Thank you.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:44.040
But I don't know how you stand that bitter taste.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.460
Yeah. They sure are bitter.

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.250
Kinda smell like grass, too.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.000
Then what'd you eat them for?

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.630
For love... I guess.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:13.210
Oh jeez, there he goes. Thinking that loving bitter
stuff makes him all cool and mature.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.580
No, I know for a fact he totally hates green peppers.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.540
It's been like that since elementary school.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:20.290
What? So he's just pretending to be a tough guy?

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:21.210
Nope.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.670
He did it to help out the person he likes.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.290
That's what he meant by "love".

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.580
Uh, no way! It's just a tough guy act!

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:31.330
Boys like him always do that!

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:32.460
Then why don't you ask him?

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.040
Hard pass! He's just gonna tease me for it!

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.920
He teases you because he likes you.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.960
Oh yeah, my mom said something like that too...

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:47.080
Nope! Forget it! There's no way that's true!

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.000
<b>Dislikes</b>

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.380
Dislikes!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.080
Something wrong? Why the big sigh?

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.500
Well...

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.170
In my breakfast this morning there was...

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:41.960
Well, I've just been feeling off ever
since I got up this morning.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:45.330
Hey. Didn't you say something about breakfast?

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.130
Nope. Nothing.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.250
Uh-huh...

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:53.670
Close call!

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:59.580
If she found out the reason I'm feeling down is because
I had to eat stupid green peppers for breakfast...

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.250
You don't like green peppers? What a baby!

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:06.960
I can't let that happen!

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.670
Let me guess, green peppers?

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.920
You had to eat something you hate
and it ruined your whole morning?

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.420
How does she know?!

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:20.500
Green peppers are pretty bitter.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.170
Wait a sec. Do you dislike green peppers, too?

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.420
They're also pretty pungent.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.830
She relates!

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:35.210
Yeah, ain't that the truth! Who in their right mind
would ever want green peppers for breakfast?

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.460
I don't mind them, personally.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:43.170
So, you hate green peppers, huh?

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.710
You have the taste buds of a little kid.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.630
She's making a fool of me!

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.960
F-fine, what about you then? Don't you have any dislikes?

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:55.500
Dislikes?

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:00.080
Well, it's not something particular.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.000
Oh yeah. She totally does.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:07.290
Okay, so I win if I manage to guess
the thing that you dislike.

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:10.540
Sure. But I don't think you'll get it right.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:15.330
Just watch, I'm gonna hit the nail on the head. And then...

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.920
Who has the taste buds of a kid now?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.880
I'll let her have it.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:23.710
Isn't it, like, super hard to choose
what kind of emoji to use?

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.000
A vegetable?

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.880
So you want some hints, huh?

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:32.960
Nope, it's not a vegetable.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.130
It's something that perks you up.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:39.630
<b>Vegetable</b>

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:39.630
<b>Vegetable</b>

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.330
What's it taste like?

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.960
Sour and refreshing, but with some sweetness to it.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:44.170
Okay, so...

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.040
Wait, hold on.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.380
You only get one more hint, okay?

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:52.540
You'll eventually get it right if
I just keep giving you hints forever.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:57.670
Nothing gets by Takagi-san.
She totally shut down the streak I had going.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:02.000
I'm gonna have to narrow it down with this last question...

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:04.710
What color is it?

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.380
Well...

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.420
It's yellow.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:09.880
YES!

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:12.380
That really limits what it could be!

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:13.710
Now to think...

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:21.920
I've got it!

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.380
The thing that you dislike is none other than...

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:31.920
pineapple!

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:32.750
Wrong.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:33.580
For real?!

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.170
I'm still curious. What's the right answer?

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:45.330
Any beverage similar to energy drinks.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:47.290
But that's not a food!

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.330
Yeah, you only asked me what I disliked.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:51.420
Besides...

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.000
I told you that it wasn't "particular".

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:58.790
You did say that...

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:00.000
Right?

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:06.380
Hey.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:11.130
Whenever the day comes that
I have the chance to cook for you...

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.500
What chance? That's not gonna happen.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.500
You never know.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:25.210
Anyway, whenever that happens
I'll make some tasty green peppers for you.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.080
Good morning!

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.670
Oh, good morning.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:30.960
Let's go pick up the handouts.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:31.710
Sure.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:36.580
So hey, I bought this book the other day
and it's super interesting.

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:39.040
No green peppers, please.

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:42.500
Gyoza.

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.210
<b>Gyoza</b>

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:45.420
Hey, Mina.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.670
Will you eat my carrots?

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:49.000
Sure thing!

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:53.790
Being picky again, Yukari?

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:56.630
You'll never get taller like that.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.830
Yeah, well, I'm taller than you anyway.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.580
Okay, let's make it a trade.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:03.420
I'll give you one of my gyoza.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:07.330
No, I can't accept that. You're doing me
a favor by eating the carrots.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.920
It's okay, because I love carrots!

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.380
Sure, but you love gyoza too, right?

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:14.880
I love pretty much anything, so no worries!

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:16.830
Really? But...

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.210
Go on, I insist!

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:20.130
No, I really shouldn't.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:21.000
Come on, take it!

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:21.960
I'm good, you have it.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:23.210
I'm giving it to you!

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:25.420
Like I said, I feel bad...

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.710
You don't hav- huh?

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:33.420
Wow. This gyoza is really good.

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:36.000
Why the heck did you eat it, Sanae-chan?!

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.130
Yeah, what do you think you're doing?

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.460
I mean, you two obviously didn't want it, so...

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:44.790
I never said that.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.210
Look, Sanae, you need to apologize.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:55.130
Sanae? Where are you going?

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:06.080
Dude, how many of those are you going to eat?

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:12.420
I'm stocking up on calories for all the energy
I'll need in tomorrow's meeting.

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:15.250
We have to decide what our class
is doing for culture fest, right?

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:16.130
Yep.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.880
I used to think the idea of a donut hole toss was best,

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:21.710
but I decided that we should do
a fried chicken cafe instead.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:23.080
Fried chicken cafe?

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:26.250
Wait, did Tsukimoto-san agree to that idea?

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.420
That doesn't matter.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:41.080
When you get down to it, I'm really the only one
who's doing all the culture fest duty work.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:46.210
So no matter what she says, I'm going
to make sure that we do a fried chicken cafe.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:45.830
Kimura! Yo! Dude!

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:47.750
And then... huh?

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:48.880
Turn around! Behind you!

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:52.130
Tsukimoto-san!

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:56.290
Uh, listen, Nishikata and Takao here
agree with me about the cafe, so...

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.040
What?!

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:58.290
Don't drag us into it!

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.920
<b>MELON</b>

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.920
<b>BREAD</b>

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:06.250
Here.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.830
Huh?! For me?!

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.630
I was wrong to assume that you didn't want the gyoza.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.500
Wow, thanks!

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.290
Whew. So Sanae does have a nice side to her.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:18.210
Yeah, so...

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.920
I'll trade you this for the rest of your gyoza.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:21.830
What?!

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.250
Play nice!

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:33.830
<b>Fried Chicken Cafe</b>

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:33.830
<b>3 Votes</b>

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:31.080
After tallying up all the votes,
our class has decided to go ahead

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.830
with our idea of putting on a play for the culture festival.

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:35.500
We did it, Yukari-chan!

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.130
Yeah!

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:38.830
<b>Audition</b>

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.830
I'm the one who will be writing the script.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:40.250
I'm going to be the director.

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:42.580
And I get to design the costumes!

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:44.080
Okay!

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:46.580
N-no... it can't be!

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:51.080
I knew this would happen. I mean,
nobody's ever heard of a "fried chicken cafe".

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.670
Which idea did you vote for, Nishikata?

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.380
Since you love it so much,
I bet you voted for the fried chicken, huh?

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.000
Only because Kimura asked me as a favor!

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:00.460
Sensei!

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:05.420
Considering the time that we have left until the event,
we should finish doing auditions today

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:08.460
and then next time we can start rehearsing.
Does that sound okay?

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:10.630
Have you already decided on the story?

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:12.170
Yeah, more or less.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.380
Listen up!

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.830
It's a love story between a prince and princess!

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:19.000
We came up with it together!

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:21.880
And it's really thrilling!

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:25.460
Long, long ago...

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:29.880
There lived a prince who was put
under a curse and turned into a frog.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:31.420
His name was Juliot.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:36.040
To avoid being seen by others, he spent many long
years cooped up in a castle in the forest.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:41.420
But one day, he has a fateful encounter with
a princess named Romiya who gets lost in the forest.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:43.830
They quickly fall in love with each other.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.080
Until the twist!

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:50.080
An evil wizard appears and
tries to tear the two lovers apart.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:52.170
So Romiya and Juliot flee!

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:56.170
And their cool animal friends come to save them!
That was my idea!

00:11:56.380 --> 00:12:00.670
To top it off, a shocking and sorrowful final scene
that will no doubt leave the audience in tears!

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:01.670
Yeah!

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:05.130
In the end...

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:07.460
What fate will they meet with?!

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.250
That sounds amazing!

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:09.960
Totally off the rails!

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:11.040
For sure.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:11.880
The villain...

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:14.170
My fried chicken... my fried chicken...

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:14.170
An evil wizard, eh?

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:19.420
Yahoo! I think everybody likes our idea!

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:20.290
Yeah!

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:22.250
So, we need to decide who will play who.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:25.210
I think the princess role would
best be filled by Takagi-san.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:31.000
She has the right qualities.
Like long, beautiful hair and a composed personality.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:32.670
We're going with Takagi-san.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:33.880
Is that okay?

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:37.460
Any objections?

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:38.130
Why not?

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:38.670
Sounds good.

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:39.330
I agree!

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:42.710
Takagi-san... playing the princess?

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:45.920
What do you think, Nishikata?

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:50.210
W-well, I'm down with it if everybody else is...

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:51.210
Oh?

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:53.500
All right, we have our princess.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:54.540
Okay!

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:58.790
The biggest problem is figuring out
who will play the frog prince.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.540
We're not sure who would be a good fit.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:02.630
And so...!

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:04.960
We're holding auditions!

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:06.420
Auditions?

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:07.580
Yep!

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.830
All the boys will come up one at a time
and perform in front of Takagi-san.

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:13.380
Whoever manages to sound
the most princely gets the role!

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:16.210
It's just like Cinderella in reverse!

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.830
A princess searching for her destined lover!

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:21.420
Oh how it sets my heart aflutter!

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:24.460
Hey Nishikata. Let's have a contest.

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:25.420
Huh?

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:30.130
If you get chosen to be the prince
in the play, then you win.

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:30.880
What?!

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:33.380
Takagi-san! Could you come up here?

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:36.750
Wait! What kind of contest is that?!

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.210
O, my beloved. Princess Romiya!

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:41.080
Yeah, that's so true.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:43.040
Fried chicken... fried chicken...

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:41.790
Next!

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:46.670
O, my beloved. Princess Romiya.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:47.710
Next!

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:50.290
O, ribbit ribbit!

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:51.000
Next!

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.750
You're going to be the evil wizard.

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:56.460
Yes! I knew it!

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:59.040
A contest is a contest.

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:03.500
I'm totally gonna knock the wind of Takagi-san's
sails by getting the role of the prince!

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:06.000
All of you guys just sound like emotionless robots!

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:09.460
You gotta make it seem like you really love the princess!

00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:11.920
It's just a contest!

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:12.750
Next!

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:15.960
Nishikata-kun, did you hear us?

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.290
Huh? Uh...

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:28.330
Well, I...

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.000
He's setting the right mood.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:32.920
Yeah!

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.790
I knew it! Just seeing these two...

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:38.040
makes my heart go pitter-patter!

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:40.380
Oh, my beloved fried chicken...

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:40.880
Huh?

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:43.290
What's the matter, Prince Charming?

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:44.040
My beloved... fried chicken...

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:45.540
Darn you, Takagi-san!

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:48.880
She must think I'm too embarrassed
to say the line out loud!

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:50.630
Then I'll give her an earful!

00:14:52.420 --> 00:14:54.040
O-oh! My...

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:55.710
My be...

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:57.960
My beloved...

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:10.710
My beloved fried chicken! How I wanted to eat you...

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:11.500
That's it!

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:12.380
What?!

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:15.830
Say that again. But this time replace
"fried chicken" with "princess".

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:18.920
My beloved princess!

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:20.630
He's perfect.

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:20.960
Huh?

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:23.080
I can feel the love surging from his words.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.630
Kimura is the prince.

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:29.710
H-hold on a sec! He doesn't seem like a frog prince at all!

00:15:29.710 --> 00:15:32.250
I think Nishikata-kun is the better choice.

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:34.080
Oh yeah! I can see it!

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:39.330
No, it's Kimura. We'll change him to a pig prince.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:41.880
A PIG PRINCE?!

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.250
Just calm down.

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:47.500
Well, you guys managed to decide on
more than I expected you would today.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:50.830
<b>ROLES</b>

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:50.830
<b>PRINCESS ROMIYA – TAKAGI</b>

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:50.830
<b>PRINCE JULIOT (PIG) – KIMURA</b>

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:50.830
<b>EVIL WIZARD – TAKAO</b>

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:50.830
<b>GOOD WIZARD – HOJO</b>

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:50.830
<b>MONKEY – SAKURAI</b>

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:50.830
<b>DOG – SHIBASAKI</b>

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:50.830
<b>PHEASANT – TAKAGAWA</b>

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:50.830
<b>DANGO DUMPLING A – NISHIKATA</b>

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:52.250
But in order to make the culture fest a success,
you're all going to have to get on the same page.

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:56.420
Everyone should work together and practice
as if they were in the lead role.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:56.000
<b>PHEASANT – TAKAGAWA</b>

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:56.000
<b>DANGO DUMPLING A – NISHIKATA</b>

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:56.000
<b>OWNER OF THE INN – MINAE</b>

00:15:56.420 --> 00:16:00.210
You came close, Nishikata. Swap a few letters
and you could have been "Prince".

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:05.210
As long as you take your role seriously,
then you can put on a good performance.

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:03.170
"Prince" and "Dumpling" don't even sound similar!

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:05.790
I don't understand how "Dumpling A" is even a real role!

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:07.250
It's a shame.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:11.750
Remember that you won't always be in school.
So this is a once-in-a-lifetime experience for you.

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:11.750
I was looking forward to hearing...
your confession of love.

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:13.830
THOSE WERE JUST LINES FROM THE PLAY!

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:15.580
Hey! Quit interrupting, Nishikata!

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.290
S-sorry, sir!

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.630
How much farther?

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.790
We'll be there soon, Takagi-san.

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:43.670
What exactly are we going to do
in a place nobody can see us?

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.380
Tell me the plan, Mister Dumpling A.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.040
Let me guess...

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:49.500
Are you going to finish confessing your love?

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:52.420
L-look, I told you its for a contest!

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:55.540
Uh-huh.

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:58.540
Look! We're here!

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:00.580
The pond!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.790
<b>Fishing</b>

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:04.830
Wow. I didn't realize there was a pond out here.

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.000
Yep!

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:09.080
It's a secret spot that Kimura told me about.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.080
And in here...

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.210
<b>FISH BAIT</b>

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:13.210
I stashed some fishing rods and bait!

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:15.830
So, is this going to be a fishing contest?

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:16.790
Exactly.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:21.250
Whoever manages to catch 5 fish
from the pond first wins.

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:23.460
Sounds good.

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:27.130
After all, you got up extra early...

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:30.250
and went to the trouble of preparing this just for me.

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:35.380
Whatever, let's get started.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:36.130
Okay!

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:38.130
Ready? Start!

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:42.080
<b>FISH BAIT</b>

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:52.170
This is kinda nice. Just us taking it easy.

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:00.040
Sure, I guess so.

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:04.170
Hey. Does this pond have any prize catches in it?

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:05.540
A prize catch?

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:10.210
Well, according to Kimura, there's
a real whopper in here somewhere.

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.460
Wow!

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:16.250
Hey. If one of us catches it,
let's make that an instant win.

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:18.960
Sure, but there's no way that's happening.

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:25.250
Anyway, if you ask me, since you're a total fishing novice
you should focus on just making one catch firs...

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:29.460
Hooray! I got one!

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:30.290
No way!

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:33.420
She got the jump on me!

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:36.630
I better come up with an idea for your penalty, huh?

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:39.960
Go ahead and celebrate while you can.

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:42.920
Because you'll have to remove
that fish from the hook by yourself.

00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:46.330
And if you can't manage that,
then you won't be catching any more!

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:49.540
Which means I might just win.

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:54.750
All right! On to the next one.

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:57.420
WHAAAT?!

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:07.500
I prep and fillet the fish that we eat at home,
so I'm used to handling them.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.250
Unfortunately for you.

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:10.750
Crap!

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:14.630
But she's only caught one!
The real showdown starts here!

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.500
Got my second one!

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:23.630
Takagi-san, you've never fished before today, right?

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:26.460
Yep! I think I'm having beginners luck!

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:29.880
Calm down. Beginners are still just beginners.

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:32.790
Her luck has to run out eventually!

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.750
I'm gonna make a comeback starting right now!

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:37.880
You've got one on your line, Nishikata!

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:47.750
Whoa! It's a big one!

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:50.880
Wait a second... this might be the whopper!

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:17.290
Aw, poo.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.380
That's too bad.

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:30.960
But I'm glad that you didn't fall in.

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:36.040
Uh-huh...

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:43.380
Your line snapped. Guess that means I win, huh?

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:45.290
S-sure...

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:47.460
That was fun!

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:53.130
My heart won't stop trying to leap out of my chest...

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:56.130
What is this?

00:20:57.420 --> 00:20:58.330
Love.

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:05.080
Huh?

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:09.330
I love koi fish. You know, like the one we just saw.

00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:19.630
O-oh, yeah... that was a big koi fish.

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:29.880
Wish I could show it my appreciation.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:33.290
I mean, it's all thanks to that koi fish...

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:35.420
that I won our contest.

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:41.380
What should I make you do this time?

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:43.960
Curse you, Takagi-san.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:46.790
I know! I have to practice my role
as princess for the culture fest.

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:48.500
So I'll have you help me.

00:21:49.630 --> 00:21:50.380
What?

00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:55.250
You can be the dumpling...
and the prince while you're at it.

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:00.670
If you say so. I did lose the contest.
